{
  "title": "Rig kit: TPU phone cases with swappable mounts, shoe foot and GoPro heads",
  "summary": "TPU cases for a Xiaomi 12T Pro, an iPhone 14 Pro Max and an iPhone 13 mini with a swappable plate (cold-shoe receiver or GoPro prongs), a cold-shoe foot with lock wheel, GoPro 3- and 2-prong heads and an accessory shoe. Everything uses GoPro and cold-shoe standards.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-27",
  "material": "TPU 95A cases (Gås); PETG plates, feet, heads and wheel for use, PLA fit test (TNT). Hardware from the kit: M5 x 20 and M3 x 16 countersunk screws with nuts, M4 x 16 countersunk as a steel core in the stud.",
  "notes": "Reviewed by four independent reviewers (functionality, durability, ergonomics, aesthetics) over three rounds, all PASS; round 4 re-checks the corrected phone list (Xiaomi 12T Pro, iPhone 14 Pro Max, iPhone 13 mini). How it works: the PETG plate sits in a pocket inside the case back, held by the phone, and fills a rounded window flush with the case. The shoe plate is a cold-shoe receiver: drop the foot into the channel, slide it toward the phone top, lock the wheel. The foot's key takes head3 (3-prong) or head2 (2-prong, for standard GoPro mounts), locked with an M3 pin; head3 can't point its knob toward the phone top, so the mount stays out of the ultra-wide camera. The prong plates give a low GoPro mount (landscape or portrait). Cases: raised button covers, corner bumpers with air channels, lens glass 0.5 mm inside the back (the 14 Pro Max needs a 4.7 mm back for its 4.18 mm camera bump; its plate is thicker). iPhone data from Apple's drawings; the Xiaomi from angled photos (+-2.5 mm), so the TPU bands (buttons + camera) print first as a fit test. Infill: functional parts 6 walls, 40 % gyroid. No supports anywhere.",
